<title>INDIA: India Reliance Capital 1996/97 net down.</title>
<headline>India Reliance Capital 1996/97 net down.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to March, 1997</p>
<p>	     (in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net Profit		     1,015.1  vs   1,109.2</p>
<p>    Total Expenditure		269.4  vs     141.5</p>
<p>    Depreciation		     459.8  vs     607.2</p>
<p>    Total income		   2,228.6  vs   2,175.5</p>
<p>    Interest and finance chgs    313.7  vs     317.1</p>
<p>    Tax				  170.6  vs	 0.5</p>
<p>    Shr (rupees)			 8.19 vs	 9.28</p>
<p>    Div (rupees)			 2.80 vs	 2.70</p>
<p>Note: Reliance Capital Ltd is a financial services company that is part of India's largest private sector firm, Reliance Industries.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom (91-22-285 2851)</p>
